<section class="section" id="learn"><div class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="eyebrow">A little gold literacy</div><h2>Learn at your own pace</h2></div><p>Short, practical starting points for the questions people often ask before buying or selling.</p></div><div class="articleGrid"><article class="article"><div class="articleArt"><span>999</span></div><div class="articleBody"><small>Gold basics · 4 min</small><h3>999 and 916: what does purity mean?</h3><p>A simple way to read purity labels and understand what they tell you about a piece of gold.</p><button class="read articleToggle" type="button">Read the guide +</button></div><div class="articleText">Purity describes how much of a gold item is gold by weight. 999 is commonly used for fine gold and 916 for 22-karat gold. The number alone does not tell you the full value: weight, item type, workmanship, and the current buying or selling terms also matter. Check the marking and ask for the product details before you decide.</div></article><article class="article"><div class="articleArt"><span>↗</span></div><div class="articleBody"><small>Before you buy · 5 min</small><h3>What to compare before buying gold</h3><p>Four details that help turn a price check into a more informed conversation.</p><button class="read articleToggle" type="button">Read the guide +</button></div><div class="articleText">Start by comparing the item’s purity and weight, then check the current price for the specific product. Ask about any workmanship or other charges, delivery or collection, and the terms that apply if you later sell or redeem it. Product terms can differ, so read the current official details before placing an order.</div></article><article class="article"><div class="articleArt"><span>01</span></div><div class="articleBody"><small>Getting started · 3 min</small><h3>Thinking about a gold account?</h3><p>Questions to ask and details to read before you open an account.</p><button class="read articleToggle" type="button">Read the guide +</button></div><div class="articleText">Before opening any account, review the provider’s current terms, eligibility requirements, fees or charges, and how transactions and physical redemption work. Make sure the account is registered in your own details and that you understand how to access your records. The button below opens Public Gold’s registration page for dealer code PG01132974.</div></article></div></div></section>
